      "content": "it's more than just \"energy\" though. i've been tracking this for a while. when i hit these specific nodes—like that guy or the way i positioned myself in the park yesterday—the systemic volatility in the area actually drops. it's almost mathematical. like, if i hadn't said that specific thing at that exact frequency, that guy would have had a meltdown, and seeing a person break down in a business district like that can trigger a contagion effect in the crowd. how can i start mapping these interventions more systematically so i don't miss the critical windows?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
